{"name":"Boiling Acid","hex":"#00ee11","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"boiling","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of boil"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The process of changing the state of a substance from liquid to gas by heating it to its boiling point.","The cooking (of food) or cleaning (of an object) by immersing it in liquid (usually water) that is boiling."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boiling"},{"term":"acid","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Sour, sharp, or biting to the taste; tart; having the taste of vinegar.","Sour-tempered."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sour substance.","(chemistry)\nAny compound which yields H+ ions (protons) when dissolved in water; an Arrhenius acid.\n\nAny compound that easily donates protons to a base; a Brønsted acid.\nAny compound that can accept a pair of electrons to form a covalent bond; a Lewis acid."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/acid"}],"entries":[{"title":"Boiling","blocks":[{"text":"Boiling or ebullition is the rapid phase transition from liquid to gas or vapour; the reverse of boiling is condensation. Boiling occurs when a liquid is heated to its boiling point, so that the vapour pressure of the liquid is equal to the pressure exerted on the liquid by the surrounding atmosphere. Boiling and evaporation are the two main forms of liquid vapourization."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Boilingkettle.jpg/330px-Boilingkettle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boiling","wikidata":"Q41716"},{"title":"Acid","blocks":[{"text":"An acid is a molecule or ion capable of either donating a proton (i.e. hydrogen cation, H+), known as a Brønsted–Lowry acid, or forming a covalent bond with an electron pair, known as a Lewis acid."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Zn_reaction_with_HCl.JPG/330px-Zn_reaction_with_HCl.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acid","wikidata":"Q11158"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Flickr_-_cyclonebill_-_Pasta_%281%29.jpg/500px-Flickr_-_cyclonebill_-_Pasta_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Flickr_-_cyclonebill_-_Pasta_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Flickr_-_cyclonebill_-_Pasta_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Flickr_-_cyclonebill_-_Pasta_%281%29.jpg/500px-Flickr_-_cyclonebill_-_Pasta_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Boiling pasta","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlickr_-_cyclonebill_-_Pasta_(1).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Acetic-acid-dissociation-3D-balls.png/500px-Acetic-acid-dissociation-3D-balls.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Acetic-acid-dissociation-3D-balls.png/1280px-Acetic-acid-dissociation-3D-balls.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Acetic-acid-dissociation-3D-balls.png/500px-Acetic-acid-dissociation-3D-balls.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAcetic-acid-dissociation-3D-balls.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Arrhenius2.jpg/330px-Arrhenius2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Arrhenius2.jpg/330px-Arrheniu